    "done_when": "At the node's base, each of these files is run three consecutive times with pytest-xdist -n 8 over the whole file, and every failing id is logged: tests/test_receipt_after_release.py, tests/test_promotion_reads_the_terminal_record.py, tests/test_follower_checks_its_owner.py, tests/test_follower_freshness.py, tests/test_crew_dispatch_arming.py, and tests/test_crew.py::test_redispatch_does_not_inherit_a_terminal_delivery. The ids the-suite-is-green-at-head §3 names are test_a_writer_that_never_stops_cannot_hang_the_folded_promotion (a 2.0 s bound, observed 2.87 to 3.99 s), test_a_terminal_record_landing_after_exit_is_folded_into_the_row (assert 1 >= 3), the follower cases with 2 to 8 s waits, test_concurrent_dispatches_arm_exactly_one_detached_producer and test_redispatch_does_not_inherit_a_terminal_delivery. For each named id, the manifest gives the bound or count it asserts at file and line, and the mechanism that bound stands for. An id that fails under load is changed to wait on the observed condition under a bound; no constant is raised past what the mechanism guarantees. Where its bound measures a real guarantee that cannot be relaxed, the manifest records the contention it measures and why, and the id is left unchanged. After the change, each changed file passes three consecutive -n 8 runs at head. No assertion is deleted. The declared negative control is executed and logged: for one changed id, restore its original fixed wait or bound in a scratch tree, run it under the same -n 8 load, and it fails. The named files show no id failing at head that passed at base. The tests/test_ledger.py id is held by a peer node and is not touched. Every log sits under the run directory, headed with revision, tree and literal command, and ends EXIT=. Each run has its own --basetemp under /tmp, deleted afterwards. Only the named test files change.",
